    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high offensive output today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (82.40) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit from prime batting order positioning and favorable dynamic platoon splits against right-handed starters. **Gunnar Henderson** leads our squad today, as his elite spot at the top of the lineup combined with the favorable matchup against Cavalli makes him our most bankable asset. **Heliot Ramos** (66.96) also warrants attention as a high-upside play; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, his 10% park factor bump and a strong 15% SP skill advantage against Severino provide a significant ceiling boost that justifies his inclusion over safer, low-variance alternatives.\n\nWhile the core is strong, we are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Kyle Tucker** (63.41), **Josh Jung** (50.11), **Jackson Merrill** (52.65), **Andy Pages** (53.66), and **Heliot Ramos**. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where **Nolan Schanuel** (48.38) narrowly missed the cut. While **Nolan Schanuel** offers a stable floor, he was sidelined in favor of the higher-scoring profiles of **Andy Pages** and **Liam Hicks**, as the optimizer prioritized their specific platoon advantages over **Nolan Schanuel**'s neutral matchup against a tough arm in Wrobleski. Elsewhere, we continue to stash the injured **Luis Robert Jr.** while keeping an eye on **Josh Lowe**, whose efficiency score remains dampened (40.03) by an unfavorable platoon split against southpaw pitching, preventing him from cracking the active roster today.",
